            <p>C-Reactive Protein Isoforms and Their Phosphocholine Complexes. This image shows the ribbon diagrams of the pentameric (A: pCRP) and monomeric (B: mCRP) isoforms of C-reactive protein. Each of the binding sites contains 1 phosphocholine moiety (magenta) and 2 calcium ions (green). Zhou HH, Tang YL, Xu TH, Cheng B.&#x000a0;C-reactive protein: structure, function, regulation, and role in clinical diseases.&#x000a0;<italic toggle="yes">Front Immunol.</italic> 2024;15:1425168. doi: 10.3389/fimmu.2024.1425168.</p>
